^Geography of Finland^

Finland’s name, *Suomi*, is theorized to come from the words for ‘swamp’, *suo*, and ‘land’, *maa*. This already gives a pretty good idea about what the country looks like, and while in general being quite flat compared to neightbouring countries, there are many unique geographical anomalies thanks to the moving glaciers of the ice age eroding the mountains and creating lakes all over the land when it melted many thousands of years ago.

In this skill you will also learn what groups Finland is part of, the names of the seas and the cardinal directions, and what neightbouring countries there are.
